From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 05:20:13 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: MADEIRA_X64_QPC_FASTPATH=1 answers an x64 module's
 QueryPerformanceCounter without leaving the emulator

RDR2 calls QueryPerformanceCounter about 40,000 times a second, each an
x64->EC transition into ntdll's RtlQueryPerformanceCounter, which
already counts in user mode (CNTVCT, converted with an offset measured
against the system call and resynced about once a second).

With MADEIRA_X64_QPC_FASTPATH=1 (off by default), the loader binds an
x64 module's import of QueryPerformanceCounter or
RtlQueryPerformanceCounter, when it resolves to ntdll's x64 export
thunk, and its import of KERNEL32's QueryPerformanceCounter by name (a
"-import" export, through KERNEL32's import of kernelbase's, which is
forwarded to ntdll's: RDR2 and its launcher import it from KERNEL32;
taking only imports that resolve to ntdll bound nothing on the phone,
nor did following the -import jump, and the first such import logs
what it resolved to), to an x64 stub in a page made per process. The stub gives what
RtlQueryPerformanceCounter gives for the same count, with its
divisions and 64-bit arithmetic: ticks(count) + offset, from the state
time.c now keeps in struct qpc_state, read while its sequence count is
even and unchanged and only within a second of the last resync. The
count is RDTSC's, shifted right by FEX's TSC scale, which the stub
reads once from CPUID 15h and keeps only when its ECX is CNTFRQ. No
state yet, a resync writing or due, or an unknown scale jumps on to
the export, which resyncs.

A resync now writes the offset and last_sync under the sequence count;
a thread that finds another one writing them leaves them to it and
uses the offset already there (its own on the first sync). A [x64-qpc]
line gives the stub's page; the [x64-cs] import line counts it with
the critical-section stubs. fex 0061 makes RDTSC self-synchronizing
under the same switch. Not covered: GetProcAddress callers.

Linear: PLA-364
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-21-x64-qpc-stub.md
Offered-upstream: no; the transition cost is the iOS port's
---
 dlls/ntdll/loader.c     | 184 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 dlls/ntdll/ntdll_misc.h |  17 ++++
 dlls/ntdll/time.c       |  42 ++++++---
 3 files changed, 232 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
index fe5a846ca78..3f904d229dc 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -1558,6 +1558,188 @@ static void *x64_cs_stub_for( HMODULE importer, const char *name, void *target )
     if (!stubs || target != targets[leave]) return NULL;
     return leave ? stubs + 0x80 : stubs;
 }
